From 33ec18b31a43a2f7a9ce5f46943344857d31c9fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: cache_salt and --cache-salt-per-key keep kept prompt states apart

A request's cache_salt (chat, completions, Responses and Messages), and
with serve --cache-salt-per-key the API key it matched, is hashed with
HMAC-SHA-256 under the server's tool-call id key and masks the first four
words of the lane host's cache key. A kept state is then resumed only by a
request with the same salt; with no salt the request is keyed exactly as
before, and tokens never change.

Salted states stay in RAM: the disk writer, reader and --learn already
refuse high-bit words, so the disk format is unchanged. A salted request
neither drafts from nor adds to Recall's record and neither reads nor
writes --compact-memory notes; the server's own requests for a salted
conversation (warm pass, compaction notes, Cortheon's planner and kept
rounds) keep the salt, and a salted /v1/imprint ask looks up its own
states. Engines whose cache is not the lane host's store refuse a salted
request with 400 and refuse to start with --cache-salt-per-key. The request
log redacts the salt, and /v1/models publishes capabilities.cache_salt.

Fixes #3196

Edited by us (lane V129B, the v1.2.9 gate): server/openai.zig is 599 lines on v1.2.9 and this commit adds
two, past the lean limit of 600. The comment above `var asked: cancel_ids.Entry = .{};` moves onto that line,
reworded to fit 120 columns (`held to the reply's end: the cancel route finds it by each id its client gets`);
no code changes.

Re-seated on the v1.2.9 engine series by work/V129B/recut_combined.py: applies to tree 3b06d167fd742683f210ffc7f69eef5199640664 (the series and
patches/pr1411); it adds and removes exactly the lines of lane V129B's pristine-v1.2.9 0001.
